### AI safeguards

1. Ground project-specific claims in authorised data.
2. Retrieve data only within the current user's permissions.
3. Clearly distinguish facts, interpretations, assumptions and recommendations.
4. Cite the relevant indicator, reporting period or source record within the application where possible.
5. State when data is missing or insufficient.
6. Never invent indicator values, quotations, field findings or evaluation conclusions.
7. Never silently modify official data.
8. Never approve submissions or reports autonomously.
9. Require human review before publication.
10. Minimise personal and sensitive data sent to external AI services.
11. Never expose API keys in client-side code.
12. Handle model errors, quotas, latency and untrusted document content safely.
13. Record the model, prompt version and relevant input-data snapshot when necessary for reproducibility.
14. Clearly label generated content as AI-assisted.

Use structured outputs and validation for machine-readable responses.

Do not assume that an AI recommendation is statistically valid merely because it sounds plausible.

