## 37. FINAL DIRECTIVE

Start by examining the existing repository and identifying the current state of every module.

Then implement the platform incrementally, preserving working functionality and resolving the highest-risk architectural issues first.

Do not stop after creating a plan, mockup, prototype, schema, or set of placeholder pages.

Do not attempt an uncontrolled rewrite of the entire codebase in one operation.

Do not invent completed functionality, test results, successful integrations or security guarantees.

If a feature requires external credentials, paid services, unavailable infrastructure or a decision that cannot safely be inferred, implement the parts that can be completed, document the dependency, and request the specific missing information.

When implementation is complete, provide an honest feature-by-feature status report identifying what is fully operational, what is partially implemented, what requires configuration, and what remains outstanding.

The objective is a reliable, integrated MEAL platform in which every major module works with the others and every official result can be traced to its data, methodology, reporting period and approval history.